{
  "_about": "Countdowns to a player's events and exams. The list is the synced setting `countdowns` (synced_settings.json holds its limits); the server only checks that it is well formed. Both clients compute what they show from the cases here. `days`: an Anki day starts at the collection's day start hour (Anki's \"next day starts at\"), so today is the local date of `now` minus `day_start_hour` hours; `days` is the event's date minus today, and `state` names it. `nearest`: the event Home and Today show, the one with the fewest days that is not past; on a tie the first in the list. `order`: the list in settings, by date and on a tie in stored order, past ones included until the player removes them. `search`: the Anki search for the cards a linked deck still has before the event (subdecks included, suspended cards left out): new, learning, and review cards due before the event day. `pace`: cards a day from today up to the day before the event, rounded up; `remaining` null means no deck is linked or the collection has no such deck. `wording`: the English text; each client translates it. `pace_one` and `pace_other` are the plural forms of one message. `import`: countdowns made while signed out stay on the device, apart from every account's list; on sign-in the client offers to add them to the account (`import_*` wording), once that account's list has synced, and only when at least one would be added. `device` is the signed-out list, `account` the account's; `expected.account` is the account's list after adding: its own events first, unchanged, then each device event in device order, unless the list already has an event with the same name and date (compared exactly; the account's deck wins) or is full. `expected.left` are the device events that did not fit; they stay on the device. Declining keeps the whole device list on the device, shown while signed out. `import_one`/`import_other` and `left_one`/`left_other` are plural forms.",
